.TH XD\-CHOOSE\-FILE 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-choose\-file \- pick a file and print its path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-choose\-file
.OP \-\-title text
.RB [ \-\-images | \-\-programs | \-\-styles | \-\-themes ]
.OP \-\-folder dir
.OP \-\-save name
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-choose\-file
is an internal helper of XeonDesktop: the Browse... buttons of Run
.RB ( xd\-run (1))
and Display Properties
.RB ( xd\-desk (1))
use it to show GTK's file chooser.
It prints the chosen file's path on standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-title " text"
The window's title (default \(lqBrowse\(rq).
.TP
.B \-\-images
Offer pictures first, then all files.
.TP
.B \-\-programs
Offer programs (executable files and desktop entries) first, then all
files.
.TP
.B \-\-styles
Offer visual styles first (Windows\(aq .msstyles and .theme files, and
XeonDesktop theme packages, .xdtheme), then all files.
.TP
.B \-\-themes
Offer themes first (Windows\(aq .theme files and XeonDesktop theme
packages, .xdtheme; with
.BR \-\-save ,
only .xdtheme), then all files.
.TP
.BI \-\-save " name"
Ask for a file to save to, with
.I name
in the box, instead of one to open; an existing file is replaced only
when the user confirms.
.TP
.BI \-\-folder " dir"
Start in
.IR dir .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XD_CHOOSE_FILE_ANSWER
For tests: printed as the answer, without showing the dialog.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when a file was chosen, 1 when the dialog was cancelled.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-run (1),
.BR xd\-desk (1)
